Stop [E3001]: `panic: expected the answer, got none`
  --> examples/features/errors/qq_panic.jet:10 in run
     |
10 |     v :: maybe() ?? panic("expected the answer, got none")
     |                     ^^^^^
 Why: The program hit a `panic`, `require`, or `require_eq` call that failed, a bounds/key check triggered at runtime, or another program-side stop. The shared report boundary owns the program-side stop; an unhandled entry error is a returned report, not E3001. Jet file and line are shown in Jet terms — never generated-Rust terms (I2).
 Fix: Fix the logic that led to the failure. Program-side stops exit 70 through the shared boundary; unhandled entry errors print their report and exit 1; exit 101 is reserved for Jet defects.
